<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="mtl_bike tools/build.py" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1 http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1/gpx.xsd">
  <metadata><name>Vermont Champlain Islands Variant</name><desc>Designed for the 7-day tour: the Local Motion bike ferry runs only Fri to Sun (plus Mon Oct 12), so the island day must fall on Fri Oct 9. On the 6-day plan this variant would make the last day about 111 mi. On the 5-day plan the island day would be a Thursday, when the bike ferry doesn't run.</desc></metadata>
  <wpt lat="44.31005" lon="-73.35154"><name>Lunch: Pink Pig Cafe</name><desc>Mile 38.9. 2750 Essex Rd, Essex, NY. (518) 962-8833. Next to the ferry dock. Hours are limited in the fall (one listing shows Fri to Sun hours and closed Mon to Wed; Thursday is unclear): call ahead. The Essex Ice Cream Cafe is summer-only, and 'The Cup Cafe' from earlier drafts does not appear to exist.</desc><sym>Restaurant</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.47891" lon="-73.21788"><name>Hotel: Hotel Vermont</name><desc>Mile 61.1. 41 Cherry St, Burlington, VT. (802) 651-0080. Downtown, near the lakefront path.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.47879" lon="-73.21860"><name>Hotel: Courtyard Burlington Harbor</name><desc>Mile 61.1. 25 Cherry St, Burlington, VT. (802) 864-4700. Next door to Hotel Vermont.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.48510" lon="-73.21030"><name>Bike: Old Spokes Home</name><desc>Mile 61.1, 0.6 mi off route. 331 N Winooski Ave, Burlington, VT. (802) 863-4475. Tue to Fri 10 to 6, Sat 10 to 5; closed Sun and Mon.</desc><sym>Bike Trail</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.47600" lon="-73.21560"><name>Bike: North Star Sports</name><desc>Mile 60.7, 0.2 mi off route. 100 Main St, Burlington, VT. (802) 863-3832. Downtown bike shop near the waterfront.</desc><sym>Bike Trail</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.04761" lon="-73.45925"><name>Food: Stewart's Shops #103</name><desc>Mile 15.6. 4308 Main St, Port Henry, NY. (518) 546-3025. Guaranteed food and water on Day 5. Top up here.</desc><sym>Convenience Store</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.04233" lon="-73.45883"><name>Station: Port Henry</name><desc>Mile 15.1, 0.1 mi off route.</desc><sym>Train</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.18717" lon="-73.45189"><name>Station: Westport</name><desc>Mile 26.2, 0.8 mi off route.</desc><sym>Train</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.81642" lon="-73.29068"><name>Lunch: Hero's Welcome General Store</name><desc>Mile 27.6. 3537 US Route 2, North Hero, VT. (802) 372-4161. Deli, bakery and general store on the lake. Standard hours Mon to Sat 7 to 6, Sun 8 to 5; hours are reduced seasonally.</desc><sym>Restaurant</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.32482" lon="-73.26641"><name>Hotel: Quality Hotel Centre de Congrès</name><desc>Mile 72.8. 725 Boul. du Séminaire N, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC. +1 (450) 300-5177. North side of town, near the canal. Choice Hotels toll-free: 1-800-667-3815.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.32391" lon="-73.26475"><name>Hotel: Auberge Harris</name><desc>Mile 72.5. 576 Rue Champlain, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC. +1 (450) 348-3821. Riverside inn close to the start of the canal path. Toll-free 1-800-668-3821.</desc><sym>Lodging</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.35408" lon="-73.29597"><name>Bike: Cycle LM</name><desc>Mile 72.8, 2.4 mi off route. 270 Boul. Saint-Luc, Saint-Jean-sur-Richelieu, QC. . Bike shop with a repair workshop, about 2.4 mi west of the route. Replaces 'Performance Bégin', which could not be found. Phone not verified: see cyclelm.com.</desc><sym>Bike Trail</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="45.01030" lon="-73.37086"><name>BORDER: Rouses Point–Lacolle 223</name><desc>Mile 47.5. Open 8 AM to 8 PM daily (both sides). Passport, EDL or NEXUS. No cannabis.</desc><sym>Crossing</sym></wpt>
  <wpt lat="44.99500" lon="-73.37117"><name>Station: Rouses Point</name><desc>Mile 46.4, 0.3 mi off route.</desc><sym>Train</sym></wpt>
  <trk><name>VT1: Ticonderoga, NY to Burlington, VT (via Essex ferry)</name><desc>61.1 mi (98.3 km), about +2,500 ft. Routed on OpenStreetMap along the official trails.</desc><trkseg>
